- Detection of recurring charges.
- UPI AutoPay and bank mandate tracking.
- Upcoming renewal reminders.
- Trial reminders.
- Unused subscription identification.
- Duplicate subscription identification.
- AI-powered financial insights.

**Implication for DebitLens:**

Automatic SMS detection, renewal reminders, unused-subscription flags and ordinary subscription dashboards cannot individually be claimed as our unique innovation.

Our differentiation must be more substantial.

### 2. Fidaura

References:

https://fidaura.innocorelabs.com/

https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.innocorelabs.fidaura

Publicly advertised capabilities include:

- Recurring charge detection.
- Price-change detection.
- Upcoming renewal information.
- CSV statement import.
- Excel statement import.
- Text-based PDF statement import.
- Bank SMS processing.
- Privacy-focused financial-data handling.

**Implication:**

Statement importing, recurring charge detection and price-increase alerts already exist in the market.

We must develop a stronger identity-resolution, cancellation and verification workflow.

### 3. Reccurra

Reference:

https://reccurra.com/features/

Publicly documented capabilities include:

- Email-based transaction capture.
- Receipt and screenshot processing.
- Manual recurring-payment entries.
- Different recurring intervals.
- Monthly and yearly expense totals.
- Upcoming renewal calendars.
- Trial reminders.
- Price-rise detection.

**Implication:**

Annual calculations, renewal calendars and price-change alerts must be treated as existing capabilities rather than novel claims.

### 4. Fold Money

Reference:

https://help.fold.money/hc/en-us/articles/22030957395858-How-do-I-track-my-recurring-expenses-on-Fold

Publicly documented capabilities include:

- Recurring expense management.
- Creating recurring expenses from connected transactions.
- Manual recurring expense creation.
- Frequency configuration.
- Payment and cancellation reminders.
- A recurring calendar showing paid, upcoming and overdue payments.

**Implication:**

A recurring-expense calendar and basic transaction-to-recurring-expense conversion are not sufficient differentiators.

### 5. Essara

Reference:

https://essara.space/

Publicly advertised capabilities include:

- Subscription tracking.
- UPI AutoPay tracking.
- Recurring bill management.
- Upcoming renewal visibility.
- Annual expense calculation.
- Manual entry and tracking.

Its published positioning is manual-first rather than automatically connecting to bank accounts or reading SMS.

**Implication:**

Our prototype must reduce manual effort through transaction interpretation and recurring-pattern analysis.

### 6. Google Pay

Reference:

https://support.google.com/pay/india/answer/10840624?hl=en

Google Pay supports UPI AutoPay management, including viewing mandate states and pausing or revoking eligible mandates.

**Implication:**

Do not claim that users cannot see or cancel their UPI mandates through existing payment applications.

### 7. PhonePe

Reference:

https://www.phonepe.com/terms-conditions/autopay/

PhonePe supports recurring mandates and their management, including modification and revocation where applicable.

**Implication:**

Basic mandate management already exists.

Our application should guide users to the appropriate provider rather than pretend to replace their payment application.

### 8. NPCI — Enhanced UPI AutoPay framework

Important official circular:

https://www.npci.org.in/uploads/UPI_OC_No_223_FY_2025_26_Enhancement_of_UPI_Autopay_88b38535cb.pdf

Circular dated October 7, 2025.

It introduced enhancements allowing users to view active UPI AutoPay mandates through their chosen UPI application and port eligible mandates between applications.

It also establishes restrictions on how mandate information obtained through the viewing functionality may be used.

**Design consequence:**

Do not build an application around an unsupported assumption that every UPI application has completely isolated mandates.

Do not scrape or misuse mandate data obtained through UPI applications.

### 9. NPCI — UPI HELP

Important official circular:

https://www.npci.org.in/uploads/UPI_OC_No_227_FY_2025_26_Introduction_of_UPI_HELP_Assistant_a.pdf

Circular dated October 8, 2025.

The UPI HELP pilot describes an assistant capable of:

- Answering digital-payment questions.
- Helping users with transaction grievance processes.
- Providing unified visibility of active UPI mandates.
- Facilitating mandate lifecycle operations through deep links to participating UPI applications.

**Design consequence:**

Do not position basic UPI mandate discovery as something that no existing infrastructure can do.

Our focus must be the wider financial commitment intelligence layer.

### 10. Payment and subscription cancellation systems

Google Play official guidance:

https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/7018481

An important documented distinction is that uninstalling an application does not cancel its Google Play subscription.

This supports an important design decision: stopping the payment authorisation and cancelling the underlying service are not necessarily the same action.

