# 13. CONFIDENCE AND EXPLAINABILITY ENGINE

Every important detection should have a human-readable explanation.

Use a deterministic heuristic score rather than presenting an arbitrary AI-generated probability.

Suggested score structure:

| Evidence dimension | Maximum points |
|---|---:|
| Recurrence interval consistency | 30 |
| Merchant identity confidence | 25 |
| Number of supporting occurrences | 20 |
| Amount-pattern consistency | 15 |
| Supporting payment or mandate evidence | 10 |
| Total | 100 |

Suggested labels:

- 80–100: High confidence.
- 60–79: Medium confidence.
- Below 60: Low confidence / review required.

These numbers are prototype scoring weights, not statistically calibrated probabilities.

The detail screen must explain why the score was assigned.

Example:

"Medium confidence because the same resolved merchant appears twice approximately one year apart, but only two annual occurrences are available."

Do not show a number without explaining it.

Store:

- Evidence source.
- Related transactions.
- Matching method.
- Detection rule.
- Score components.
- Explanation.

